WEBVTT

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.760
Ichi-san, there’s still some left.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:37.760
Here.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.480
You pour delicious sake, Okinu.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.950
You got that right.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.110
Take a look.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.500
They’re so beautiful and magnificent.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:06.750
The scar from that burn is the same shape as a maple leaf, right?

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.710
Did that cheer you up?

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.720
I’ll spar with you.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.760
Yaichi, we need to prepare for the banquet.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.990
The mistress is pregnant.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:42.510
You going home?

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:49.250
How about having another round with me?

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.260
I’m already tipsy.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.330
I passed by this place the other day.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.740
I wanted to come check it out.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.990
This place isn’t you.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.510
Yaichi, huh?

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.560
That name takes me back.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:28.440
A servant named Yaichi lived in the Sawai Estate next door to my parents.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.450
But he’s dead now.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:37.710
The household he served for, the Saegusas, had one kid.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:42.460
He was a fine looking boy... named Seinoshin.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:48.320
I’d like to have a few drinks with an adult Seinoshin.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.900
Do you want to talk to someone about your past?

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.360
You also have a past, right?

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:02.690
Don’t you ever want to share your past over a few drinks?

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:06.120
I don’t have a past that I wish to discuss.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.940
So what happened to that kid?

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.550
He died. From an epidemic.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.820
Yaichi died soon after that.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.810
He fell into a well.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.640
Stupid, huh?

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.520
But that wasn’t like Yaichi at all.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.840
I suspected something at that time...

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:54.000
Seinoshin who suddenly died... then Yaichi’s corpse was taken from a well soon after that.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.450
Seinoshin was adopted by my neighbors who didn’t have a heir.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.180
Then they gave birth to a boy.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:14.150
Perhaps because of the successorship issue,
they killed Seinoshin and said he died from an illness.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.610
And Yaichi was killed in return for knowing that.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:28.620
The Saegusas’ son eventually died, and they fell into ruin after a series of misfortunes.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:34.340
It’s no use investigating those events now. It’s not going to bring them back.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.840
Not Yaichi.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.540
Nor Seinoshin.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:06.330
Someone in your family planned this “kidnapping.”

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.810
It’s a farce.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:14.640
So, my mother planned this.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.250
Right.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.380
When I threatened the guy who
approached us, he told me everything.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.810
I’m not going to kill you.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.350
I dislike pointless bloodshed.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.940
Will you come with us as well?

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.650
You have no other place to go.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:54.360
I’ll go home. Yaichi’s there.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.000
Who’s Yaichi?

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.240
A servant.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.620
He will protect me.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.690
Yaichi, huh?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:09.470
The name of the guy who approached us was Yaichi.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.880
Hmm? So Ichi-san left?

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.660
Mm-hmm.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:52.140
But he looked so pale and unhealthy today.

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:55.010
He’s always like that.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.450
No, today was different.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:02.080
It’s like he was thinking of past events.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.180
Past events?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.730
Mm-hmm.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:11.150
Welcome!

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:13.700
Hey, Matsu.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.610
Did you come worrying about Ichi, too?

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:20.310
Ichi-san? Not really.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.000
Sake!

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.660
Okay! I’ll get some snacks, too.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:25.670
No need.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:29.870
Say...

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.430
What does Ichi want to do with the Five Leaves?

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.730
Who knows?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.270
He probably doesn’t even have a particular goal.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:46.690
You know, Ume, guys like Ichi-san avoid things they don’t enjoy.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.320
Here.

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.660
Even having Masa join...

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.320
...was all just fun and games to Ichi-san.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.100
Are you seeing something?

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.360
What can you see in this darkness?

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:01.680
I’m staring because I don’t see a thing.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.340
So we meet again, Sei.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:28.710
Matsu-dono.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:30.490
What’s going on?

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.570
I’m waiting since Ichi-san isn’t here.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:38.080
Yaichi-dono hasn’t returned?

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.130
Is it something urgent?

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:43.690
No. I was just a little worried.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.720
I’m heading back.

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.950
I will also go search for him for a bit.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.200
Come here.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:06.580
My, you’re heavy.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.100
You sure know how to live well.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.440
I’ve heard through the grapevine.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.190
It seems...

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:37.180
...that Monji died a little while back.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.020
Did you kill him?

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:44.600
Sei.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.650
It was you, wasn’t it?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:01.090
You weren’t satisfied with selling out the Kuhei of the Bakuro crew to the city.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:09.520
I’ll tell you something before you die.

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:17.240
Sei, the guy who made the arrangements for your family wasn’t named Yaichi.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:28.290
We didn’t even...

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:33.640
...hear of his name in the first place.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:28.850
But if we didn’t tell you that, you...

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.900
...would have been killed.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.620
They’re so beautiful and magnificent.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:23.090
Yaichi...

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:47.340
Yaichi-dono.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:59.440
So you were here.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:47.030
Yaichi-dono?

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:53.990
The snow quit falling a while ago.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:49.560
Are you coming in or not? Geez!

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.010
Welcome!

00:18:58.520 --> 00:18:59.950
Um...

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:04.330
Ichi didn’t come. You’re in the way, so sit down.

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.480
Right...

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:13.790
Yaichi-dono did not return this morning.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.910
I’m really worried about how he’s doing.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:19.490
You don’t need to worry.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.540
Why is that?

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:23.270
Ah! Matsu-san!

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:25.980
What is it?

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:32.180
Ichi-san says he wants to do
another job after the new year.

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:35.180
You’ve met with Yaichi-dono?

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.890
Yeah. Just a while ago.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.740
Where?

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.720
At the shrine he frequents.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:45.770
I’ll be going.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.200
And?

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:56.570
He asked if we would help.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:00.530
It’s not like him.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:05.660
Excuse me.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.320
What’s your business?

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:13.630
Hmm?

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:19.080
Oh... Would it be possible to buy some sake in this shop?

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.450
A customer?

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.890
Come in!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:54.160
Anything is delicious if you’re hungry.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:35.990
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:45.280
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:53.700
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:22:00.750
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:09.680
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:17.760
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:26.580
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:34.820
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:43.930
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high
